@startuml
'==== Title ====
title "As a Buyer, I want to use the Web UI to bid on an auction." - SD %n()

'==== basic style ====
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Futura
skinparam objectFontSize 20
skinparam backgroundColor CornSilk
skinparam objectBackgroundColor WhiteSmoke
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFE0
skinparam ArrowFontColor #3B4953
skinparam ActivationBackgroundColor black
hidefootbox
autonumber

' ==== Actor and participants ====
actor User
participant ":Frontend" as FE
participant ":Backend" as BE

note over FE
Assumes the user already opened the Auction
they want to bid on, via GET /auctions/{auctionId}.
To know what actions are allowed on that auction,
the Frontend calls OPTIONS /auctions/{auctionId},
whose response includes a "place-bid" link pointing
to /auctions/{auctionId}/bids. That href is what
"Frontend" follows below, not a hardcoded URL.
end note

User -> FE : I want to place a bid for %n() x value on an auction.
activate FE
note over FE
currency is predetermined
by the auction's starting
price currency
end note
FE -> BE : OPTIONS /auctions/{auctionId}
activate BE

ref over BE
[[rest-sd-ref-diagrams/OPTIONS_Place_Bid_SD.puml OPTIONS for user on /auctions/{auctionId}]]
end ref

BE --> FE : 200 OK + [GET, POST]
note over BE
This POST means the user may place a bid
by sending a request to the place-bid href
(/auctions/{auctionId}/bids).
end note
deactivate BE

FE -> BE : POST {place-bid href} %n(){ placeBidRequestDTO } + %n()userIdFromHeader
activate BE

ref over BE
[[rest-sd-ref-diagrams/POST_Place_Bid_SD.puml POST (place bid on auction)]]
end ref

BE --> FE : 201 Created + bidResponseDTO
deactivate BE
FE --> User : Bid successfully %n() placed on auction.
deactivate FE

@enduml